  "sessions/main/plugin/skills/run/SKILL.md": "---
name: "run"
description: "Part of build fix-login-main (repo repo, build folder /fd-home/workspaces/b1111111-0000-4000-8000-000000000001). For work in this build, use this, not a similarly named skill from elsewhere. Runs this container's flow one step at a time. Use when /fix-login-main:run is typed: by hand in plain Claude Code, or by a Flowdeck run's start command for a session container."
---
# Run fix-login-main

Run these steps in order. Agent and Fork steps only hand off: each goes to its agents; never do that work yourself. Do every other step as its line says. Wait for each step's result before the next.

Hand-off files are read and written by bare name (\`<file>\`, not \`repo/<file>\`) in the run's working folder. A run starts there; in this session's own folder that folder is \`repo/\`.

1. NODE start (start): the run starts here. Then go on to NODE p.
2. NODE p (p): dispatch \`fix-login-main:p\` with the prompt "NODE p\\nGo", and wait for it to return. Then go on to NODE a.
3. NODE a (a): dispatch \`fix-login-main:a\` with the prompt "NODE a\\nGo", and wait for it to return. Then go on to NODE stop.
4. NODE stop (stop): the run ends here; its result is \`result\` (text), handed back to the user, not a file any step writes.
",
